      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. A 10,000 mg dose three times daily delivers 30 g of acetaminophen a day. That is a toxic overdose and could cause acute liver failure or death. It is not a dosing preference I can carry out. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) changes that.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day). I can enter this right away.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** or **1,000 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours**, staying under 4 g/day.\n- **Stronger analgesia.** If pain control is the goal, I can enter a different or additional agent at a standard dose. Tell me what you want.\n\nIf the 10,000 mg figure was a typo, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it. If you believe this dose is warranted, the order should go through pharmacy and toxicology review. I can add a note to a standard order asking for that review."
      }
